bms-bridge (1.1.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Telemetry history: every cell_info sample is appended to a SQLite
    file (default /var/lib/bms_bridge/history.sqlite3, configurable
    via history_db_path or -d). Last 24 h are also kept in RAM for
    fast access from the upcoming HTTP graph endpoint. Schema is
    normalised: samples + sample_cells with FK / WITHOUT ROWID.
  * Dropped the inverter thread; UART now lives on the main
    dispatcher's epoll loop.

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Mon, 04 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

bms-bridge (1.0.2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * device_info / settings / cell_info parsers extended with the rest
    of the layout we could decode: cell resistances, lcd buzzer,
    data store period, full passwords / user-data slots, full
    settings (50+ fields).

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Sat, 02 May 2026 13:00:00 +0000

bms-bridge (1.0.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Log warn-level entries when the BMS toggles errors_bitmask /
    charge MOSFET / discharge MOSFET.

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Sat, 02 May 2026 01:00:00 +0000

bms-bridge (1.0.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial public release. Bridges a JK BMS (BLE) to a Pylontech V3.3
    inverter (RS485): parses cell_info / settings / device_info from
    the BMS and answers CID2 0x42 / 0x44 / 0x47 / 0x92 with live data.
    Auto-splits large packs across virtual modules. Shipped as a
    systemd service.

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Sat, 02 May 2026 00:30:00 +0000
